P8-tune.F PR-0 (#394) — Mac local memory-safety smoke

Platform constraint note
========================
valgrind has no Apple Silicon / Darwin AArch64 port (upstream issue: no Darwin
ARM64 host support; last attempt 2021 stalled on Mach trap dispatch). On Mac
the equivalent gate is AddressSanitizer (ASan) + UBSan via `make shud_asan`.

Per CLAUDE.md "all alternative tooling documented", this evidence file
substitutes Mac shud_asan run for the spec-named valgrind step. The Linux
server (frd_muziyao@210.77.77.22) DOES have valgrind; the canonical valgrind
keliya/heihe run is deferred to orchestrator Phase 2 server validation
(see server_acceptance_cmds.sh in the same evidence directory).

Mac ASan + UBSan post-fix run
==============================
Build:
  cd SHUD && make shud_asan       # SHUD_ASAN_FLAGS=-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer

Invocation:
  cd SHUD/Basins/keliya
  rm -rf output/keliya.out
  ASAN_OPTIONS="detect_leaks=0:halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1" \
  UBSAN_OPTIONS="print_stacktrace=1:halt_on_error=1" \
    ../../shud_asan keliya

Result:
  EXIT=0
  ASan errors (grep -c 'AddressSanitizer.*ERROR'): 0
  UBSan errors (grep -c 'runtime error|UndefinedBehavior.*ERROR'): 0
  Sanitizer warnings (grep -c '*Sanitizer.*WARNING'): 0
  Stdout tail: "The successful end." + Final Statistics (lenrw/leniw/nst/nfe/nfeLS/...)
  Stderr: empty (no sanitizer output = clean run)

Note on `detect_leaks`
======================
Mac ASan does not support `detect_leaks=1` (LeakSanitizer Darwin port absent):
  ==XXXX==AddressSanitizer: detect_leaks is not supported on this platform.
On Linux GH runner the flag flip from 0→1 produces `LEAK SUMMARY:` stderr line;
that path is gated in `.github/workflows/serial-baseline.yml` `asan-ubsan (keliya)`
job via the P8-tune.F PR-0 ASAN_OPTIONS env change (this PR). The CI runner is
the canonical LEAK SUMMARY emission site.

Bitwise neutrality vs pre-fix baseline
=======================================
Compare pre-fix vs post-fix SHA256 on keliya rivqdown.dat:

  pre-fix SHA  = b769e3270e1c4d075e7913bf0d0a229530200ae4b11663bdfa4a0cc3c9c028bd
  post-fix SHA = b769e3270e1c4d075e7913bf0d0a229530200ae4b11663bdfa4a0cc3c9c028bd

MATCH → fix is bitwise-neutral by construction (NSDMI nullptr defaults are
immediately overwritten by the existing `new` assignments in
Model_Data::malloc_EleRiv() / MD_Lake.cpp / MD_readin.cpp; only failure-path
behavior changes from UB → defined-no-op).

